## What to build

Turn an execution approval into a clean, isolated feature baseline. Verify Git state and selected commit, create the feature integration branch and baseline worktree, prepare its environment, and run configured checks. Record failures without charging an issue attempt. Introduce the shared run-local validation skip policy needed for baseline timeouts, then expose readiness through OpenCode status.

## Context: files to read before implementing

- `PRD.md` (lines 88–97): numbered user stories used in this ticket.
- `PRD.md` (lines 181–187): clean checkout, selected commit and baseline rules.
- `PRD.md` (lines 144–152): repository identity and durable operation intent.
- `PRD.md` (lines 211–225): timeout skip policy.
- [Implementation conventions and graph](README.md): proposed common interfaces, test commands, and greenfield constraints.
